From 8c783e717b839b0e511820e89d29840cae0f3c0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:23:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(launch): supervise configured child and exec lifecycles

Own bounded process identities and descriptor snapshots before children
run. Join fork, image exec, child waits and signals to shared filesystem,
device and pipe ownership; drain descendants when init exits.

Commit CLOEXEC retirement only after successful exec, preserve public
state on failure, and validate kernel-selected interpreter authority.
Keep typed child outcomes and all-or-nothing TID/status writes while
reaping children even when wait status copyout faults.

Signed-off-by: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
